  icon: {fileID: 0}
  title: OUTLINE USE
  prevReadme: {fileID: 0}
  nextReadme: {fileID: 0}
  sections:
  - name: Header -Intro
    heading: Intro
    text: Hi , this readme is to teach you how to use the different outline in the
      unity scene.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - name: Header -Outline 2D
    heading: Outline 2D
    text: The M_Outline 2D put an outline on 2D object , you can change the color
      and the thickness. No need to put something in the maintex_ section but if
      needed make sure to put the right texture for your object.aaa
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - name: Header -3D Outlin...
    heading: 3D Outline Black
    text: "This outline is normally only for the 3D object. \nBEWARE : it is a fullscreen
      shader so it applies on everything that the camera sees.\nIF A 2D OBJECT HAS
      THE OUTLINE : Select your 2d prefab and go to layers (above right) and in LAYER
      , select 2D, normally after, the outline dissapears.\n"
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - name: Header -3D Outlin...
    heading: 3D Outline White
    text: "This outline is normally only for the 3D object. \nBEWARE : it is a fullscreen
      shader so it applies on everything that the camera sees.\nIF A 2D OBJECT HAS
      THE OUTLINE : Select your 2d prefab and go to layers (above right) and in LAYER
      , select 2D, normally after, the outline dissapears.\n"
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - name: Header -3D Outlin...
    heading: 3D Outline Simple
    text: 'This outline is a basic outline for 3D Objects

      HOW TO USE IT: 
      Select your 3D object or prefab ; in meshrenderer add a material and add the
      outline simple

      BEWARE : it technically dubplicate the object to create
      the outline so use carefully.

'
    linkText: 
    url: 
  isRoot: 0
